Recorded transcripts land here, one file per scenario and seed.

Empty on purpose. The six files that used to sit here were hand-written
fixtures, not recordings: all three seeds of each were byte-identical, and one
called get_failure_risk(machine_id=42, as_of="2015-11-15T06:00:00") -- a
test-split prediction time -- against a scenario that had been rewritten to
machine 30 at 2015-10-14. It scored passed=True for answering a different
question. evals/transcript.py now refuses both mistakes.

Record with:  python -m evals.record --provider ollama
